---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="About" description={`About ${site.name} and how we work.`}>
  <section class="hero hero--page">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A small practice focused on infrastructure that lasts.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        {site.name} works with operations and engineering teams on cloud infrastructure, devops,
        network, automation and edge security.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name} is led by Arvind Konar, a Staff Site Reliability Engineer with more than ten
        years across SRE, cloud infrastructure, Kubernetes, networking and security. The work
        here comes from running production systems, not only designing them.
      </p>
      <p>
        Day to day that has meant building automated multi-cloud platforms on AWS, Google Cloud
        and Azure, defined in Terraform and delivered through GitOps pipelines. It has also meant
        designing the networks underneath them, from VPCs, VPNs and transit routing to BGP, load
        balancers and firewalls, and standing up the observability stack on top with Prometheus,
        Grafana, Loki and OpenTelemetry. On the network side the background includes Juniper,
        Cisco, Arista, Palo Alto and F5, with Python and Ansible automation. At the edge it is
        Cloudflare Zero Trust, WAF and DNS.
      </p>
      <p>
        We work best with engineering and operations teams that already ship software and want
        their infrastructure to be as reviewable and repeatable as their code: platform teams,
        growing product companies, and network groups moving from manual change to automation.
      </p>

      <h2>How we work</h2>
      <p>
        We prefer small, well-defined engagements with a clear outcome. Work happens in your
        repositories and your accounts, through your review process, so there is nothing to
        migrate when we finish.
      </p>
      <p>
        We write things down. Every engagement ends with documentation and runbooks your team can
        use, and time set aside to walk your engineers through what was built and why.
      </p>

      <div class="actions">
        <a class="button" href="/contact/">Start a conversation</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
